  "scientific_status": "The manuscript constructs the complete charged/neutral common-J finite-time memory covariance AA+AB+BA+BB in the stated model and limit. Complex charge tilt identifies the joint charge-energy regression; same-sample mixed Grams give strong residual reduction, fixed-field spectral absolute continuity controls exact energy pinching, and summable time tails give the convergent full kernel. The bulk de Sitter dictionary remains the next physical problem.",
  "parameters": "Standard CAR, overlapping complex Gaussian p-body model, same J across charge sectors, normalized annealed beta=mu=0 full-Fock trace, hbar=1/string time; even N, p to infinity, lambda_N=p^2/N to positive lambda, fixed Js. Polynomial degrees and real s,u,T are fixed before the double-scale limit.",
  "proof_scope": "Finite exact graph/CAR checks, complex-source comparisons and coefficient quadratures validate their recorded interfaces. They do not substitute for the manuscript arbitrary-degree joint regression, positive-measure limit, pinching and time-resummation proofs. The infinite spectral density is L1; fixed-field L2 density bounds are not claimed uniform in field degree. Uniformity for all external real T applies to series tails, not finite-N spectral convergence. No growing-time or simultaneous small-lambda limit is taken.",
  "continuation": "Use the constructed spectral matrix to test the Susskind de Sitter mass/position and bilocal dictionary, while checking the remaining A1 naming calibration. Finite-temperature, uniform small-lambda and finite-G four-point interpretations are separate questions, not consequences of this covariance proof.",
